2403|n|The plank, stone, or piece of timber, which lies under a door, especially of a dwelling house, church, temple, or the like; the doorsill; hence, entrance; gate; door. ; Fig.: The place or point of entering or beginning, entrance; outset; as, the threshold of life.	a:17zd,55,10;bwc,44,4;1xt5,8,4~17zd,55,10;1xt5,8,4;bwc,44,4	v:1rb7,58,6~1rb7,58,6	n:1ucy,83,16~1ucy,83,16
